    "summary": "A woman&#039;s skirt wrap, a &#039;katrinca&#039;.  Rectangular in shape, with a solid black centre [62 cm wide] bordered by solid black and multicoloured panels.  Twill woven [2/2 twill] by hand from wool, with the selvedges worn at the waist and hem.  The two bordering panels [33 cm approx] have alternating black wool and multicoloured wool and cotton stripes (woven as bands): green, pink, yellow and purple woollen thread and lilac cotton thread.  The warp ends are turned and blanket stitched with red wool.  Some marks in the black centre field.",
